= The Assembly Reconvenes

With DuFour making it clear that he expects a parliamentary cabinet from Trevannon, the Chancellor has moved to significantly broaden the governing coalition—reaching well to the left. The biggest surprise is the return of Askew as Foreign Minister.

Though Trevannon and his allies are interested in taming the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, the <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**DSU**</span> has no interest in becoming a junior partner in a partisan conservative government.

Trevannon inaugurated his new cabinet within the last week, drawing ministers from the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ASPD**</span> on the left to his own party on the right. Still, this patchwork coalition is unlikely to command a majority—and a vote of no confidence looms.

- @reichstag_yay
- @reichstag_nay

@reichstag_yay
title: Vote for the motion of no confidence, forcing new elections to be called.
subtitle: New elections again?
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.heartland_leader == "Crowde") Q.heartland_leader = "Goodlake";
if (Q.vice_chancellor == "Crowde") Q.vice_chancellor = "Sedgewick";

Q.next_election_week = Q.week + 6;
Q.next_election_month = Q.month;
Q.next_election_year = Q.year;
Q.next_election_time = Q.time;

let added_months = Math.floor(Q.next_election_week / 4);
Q.next_election_month += added_months;
Q.next_election_time += added_months;
Q.next_election_week = Q.next_election_week % 4;
if (Q.next_election_week === 0) Q.next_election_week = 1;

if (Q.next_election_month > 12) {
    Q.next_election_month -= 12;
    Q.next_election_year += 1;
}
!}

As expected, Trevannon isn't able to conjure up a majority without the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> or <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**DSU**</span>. His government remains a caretaker for the time being.

New Assembly elections are scheduled for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +], Week [+ next_election_week +].

@reichstag_nay
